    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u help me understand this part of an nda i just got? it says: \"The Receiving Party shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Disclosing Party from and against any and all losses, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or resulting from any breach of this Agreement or any unauthorized use of the Confidential Information by the Receiving Party or its Representatives.\" basically what does this mean for me if i mess up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This clause means that if you or anyone acting on your behalf (like employees or contractors) breaches the NDA or misuses the confidential information, you are personally responsible for covering all resulting costs, damages, and legal fees for the other party. In practical terms, if a leak or unauthorized use happens, you could be on the hook for their attorneys' bills and any financial losses they incur—not just your own. It shifts the financial risk entirely to you, so you’d want to be very careful about how the information is handled and ensure everyone you work with follows the same rules.",
